## Dark RTL Dashboard Rules

- **Preserve the dark RTL admin theme.** Do not change the admin visual system without explicit approval.
- Use **RTL-safe logical CSS properties** instead of directional hardcodes:
  - `margin-inline-start` / `margin-inline-end` instead of `margin-left` / `margin-right`
  - `padding-inline` / `padding-block` instead of `padding-left` / `padding-right`
  - `inset-inline-start` / `inset-inline-end` instead of `left` / `right`
  - `text-align: start` / `end` instead of `left` / `right`
- Avoid hardcoded `left` / `right` in new CSS; the admin already has RTL class toggles.

### Table columns

- Every table column must carry an **intentional alignment class** (text-start, text-center, text-end).
- Status, toggle, and action columns must be explicitly aligned (typically `text-center`).

### Toggle / switch

- A toggle/switch must **visually differentiate active vs inactive** state (color, background, icon).
- Do not render a toggle that always looks the same regardless of model value.

### Create / edit forms

- Use **consistent Bootstrap column sizes** (`col-md-6`, `col-md-4`, `col-md-12`) for form field grids.
- Avoid single-field rows unless the field is intentionally full width (e.g., textarea, rich editor).

### Labels

- All visible admin UI labels must use **translation keys** (`__('admin/main.name')`) — never raw key strings or hardcoded labels.
- The only exception is `<x-form.*>` component labels, which accept plain keys (e.g. `'name'`) because the component resolves the translation internally.

### Select / toggle edit state

- When rendering a `<select>` or toggle for a **boolean or status field**, the current model value must be correctly `selected` / `checked` in the edit page.
- Verify that `old()` fallback does not override the model value on edit forms.
